{
  "id": "ep152",
  "duration": 49.995,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.48,
      "text": "A comet once shone so brightly astronomers studied it in broad daylight.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "C-west-1976-ps.jpg",
        "credit": "J. Linder/ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C-west-1976-ps.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 3.067,
          "end": 4.467,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.48,
      "end": 14.225,
      "text": "Discovered photographically by astronomer Richard M. West on August tenth, 1975, the magnificent sungrazer plummeted toward our star.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.467,
          "end": 14.233,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 14.225,
      "end": 22.47,
      "text": "By February twenty-fifth, 1976, the cosmic visitor raced within exactly thirty million kilometers of the Sun.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Guide leaflet (1901) (14765710404).jpg",
        "credit": "Internet Archive Book Images",
        "license": "No restrictions",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guide_leaflet_(1901)_(14765710404).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 14.233,
          "end": 19.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.833,
          "end": 22.467,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 22.47,
      "end": 28.94,
      "text": "Intense solar heating pushed its peak apparent magnitude to minus three, easily rivaling Venus.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "C2020F3 (NEOWISE) from Estonia 2.jpg",
        "credit": "Taavi Niittee",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C2020F3_(NEOWISE)_from_Estonia_2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 22.467,
          "end": 25.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 25.9,
          "end": 28.933,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.94,
      "end": 38.01,
      "text": "Observers watched in absolute amazement from February twenty-fifth to twenty-seventh as the dazzling object was clearly viewed under a full sun.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "C-west-mar1976-ps.jpg",
        "credit": "P. St\u00e4ttmayer/ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C-west-mar1976-ps.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.933,
          "end": 33.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 33.467,
          "end": 38.0,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 38.01,
      "end": 44.73,
      "text": "Brutal tidal forces soon shattered the wandering ice block into four distinct pieces out in space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Hubble Provides Spectacular Detail of a Comet's Breakup (2006-18-1902).jpg",
        "credit": "Hubble Images (top): , , H. Weaver (JHU/APL), M. Mutchler and Z. Levay (); Ground-Based Image (bottom): G. Rhemann and M. Jager",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hubble_Provides_Spectacular_Detail_of_a_Comet%27s_Breakup_(2006-18-1902).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 38.0,
          "end": 42.233,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 42.233,
          "end": 44.733,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 44.73,
      "end": 49.645,
      "text": "This daytime record proves comets can brilliantly outshine the daytime sky.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "C-west-1976-ps.jpg",
        "credit": "J. Linder/ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C-west-1976-ps.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 44.733,
          "end": 50.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
